d powers to stop  violating an arms embargo aimed at  curbing a bloody civil war in Libya the  UN's deputy special envoy for Libya  spoke out about the problem after  meeting today with foreign ministers in  Munich she says several countries  backing rival factions in Libya have  repeatedly violated the UN backed  embargo she called for them to be held  to account I think on numerous occasions  the arms embargo has become a joke and  so it you know we all really need to  step up here Libya is awash and weaponry  and now advanced weaponry and that's  very dangerous for regional peace and  security not to mention international  peace and security  Libya has been in turmoil since 2011  when a civil war led to the downfall and  death of dictator Muammar Qaddafi  countries with interests in the war  including Turkey and the United Arab  Emirates renewed a pledge today to  uphold the arms embargo still ahead a  new way for investors to stake their  claim in the art world for a fraction of  the cost for anyone interested in owning  a piece of high-priced  art for a fraction of the cost it may be  possible a New York company is buying  artwork and then selling shares in it to  its customers there's profit potential  but it isn't limited to art in the past  few years these fractional ownership  structures have sprung up for vintage  cars racehorses and comic books  Ross Lorde reports the art world is full  of high priced products this is an 1881  landscape by Claude Monet  one of our one of our favorite offerings  that's available now so this is an  important seven million dollar painting  that were that we're offering to  investors as of recently don't have  seven million bucks kicking around not  necessary not anymore a New York startup  is billing itself as the first company  that allows anyone to invest in  multi-million dollar paintings for as  little as $1,000 American we have thirty  six thousand investors signed up today  so investors range from from very small  inve