 kidney problems over  the last few weeks he was reportedly in  hospital due to complications from  kidney disease kidney disease is on the  rise in Canada and so is the demand for  organ donations according to the latest  data from the canadian organ replacement  register there were over 1,700 kidney  transplants in 2018 in that same year  over 3,000 people were still on the wait  list and the average wait time for a  transplant is four years but this week  one man is finally getting the gift of  life and it's all thanks to friendship  Stephan Gillis and Michael Teigen spend  a lot of time together and they're just  hours away from sharing a different kind  of bond one is giving the other a kidney  I know it's not a cure it's a treatment  but it's a huge treatment to get me out  of the dialysis chair Gillis has a rare  disease that attacked both his kidneys  on top of having Crohn's disease  what yeah last April Tegan a friend  Gillis hadn't seen in a decade surprised  him with the promise of his kidney  Gillis has gone through surgeries to  prep him for the transplant while  enduring dialysis what has been the  hardest part going through what you've  had to go through or the anticipation of  this surgery mentally it's it's really  difficult all this attention has been  overwhelming just the whole experience  also just trying to understand you know  how amazing Michael is for doing this  and knowing that there's other people in  need it's not just me and but I'm the  one that's getting it it's hard to  accept sometimes so sometimes comes with  a little bit of guilt because you know  there's other people that need help 10  months later they're on track for  surgery whereas Tegan calls it a kidney  relocation was there ever a moment when  you thought I can't do this absolutely  not  no nothing more to say it's been full  steam the whole time  studies show that those who received  living organs have longer functioning  kidneys but it's not easy to be that  person who 